.TH JENT_READ_ENTROPY 3 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "Library Functions Manual"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jent_read_entropy, jent_read_entropy_safe \- generate random numbers with the CPU Jitter RNG
.SH LIBRARY
Jitter RNG library
.RI ( libjitterentropy ", " \-ljitterentropy ).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <jitterentropy.h>
.sp
.BI "ssize_t jent_read_entropy(struct rand_data *" entropy_collector ",
.BI "                          char *" data ", size_t " len );
.sp
.BI "ssize_t jent_read_entropy_safe(struct rand_data **" entropy_collector ",
.BI "                               char *" data ", size_t " len );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR jent_read_entropy ()
generates a random bit stream and returns it to the caller.
.IR entropy_collector
is the CPU Jitter entropy collector instance which shall be used
to obtain random numbers.
.IR data
is the destination memory location where the random bit stream
is written to. The memory must have already been allocated by the
caller.
.IR len
is a length value provided by the caller indicating the number
of bytes the CPU Jitter Random Number Generator shall generate.
The caller can provide any value greater than 0. The caller
must ensure that
.IR data
is at least as big as
.IR len
indicates. The function returns the number of bytes generated
when the request is successfully completed. In case of an error, one of
the negative error codes listed under
.B ERRORS
is returned.
.LP
Health test failures are reported only in FIPS or NTG.1 mode. Outside them,
.BR jent_read_entropy ()
never returns an RCT, APT, lag or RCT-with-memory error.
.LP
When a health test failure is reported, the Jitter RNG will not
have any data provided in
.IR data .
The entropy collector instance will remain in error state. To recover,
the entropy collector instance
.B MUST
be deallocated and a fresh instance must be allocated. It is
recommended that you increase the
.IR osr
value at least by one when newly allocating the Jitter RNG with
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3)
which implies that the health tests are less sensitive due to the
fact that the assumed entropy rate of the noise source is lower.
.LP
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
is a service function to and therefore operates identically to
.BR jent_read_entropy ()
with the exception that it automatically re-allocates the entropy collector
if an intermittent health test failure is reported, which happens in FIPS or
NTG.1 mode only. Before reallocation, a
new power-on health test is performed. The allocation of the new entropy
collector automatically increases the OSR by one. This is done based
on the idea that a health test failure indicates that the assumed
entropy rate is too high.
.LP
Where the noise source does not let it recover - the OSR would exceed its
maximum, or the replacement fails its own startup - the collector is out of
service for good and the failure is returned as a permanent one: the
permanent failure the replacement's startup ended in, or else the
.B *_PERMANENT
counterpart of the intermittent failure, which later calls then report as
well. Where the platform cannot provide the replacement - no memory, or a
counting thread for the internal timer that cannot be started - the
intermittent failure is returned and the collector is left as it was, and the
next call tries again; that is the only intermittent failure it returns. A
replacement on the internal timer where fewer than two CPUs are online is not
such a case: the counting thread needs a CPU of its own, which a later call
does not find either, so the failure is returned as a permanent one. Where the self tests
that precede the replacement's startup - of the conditioning or of the timer
GCD analysis - fail, the collector is
taken out of service as by a failed bound
.BR jent_selftest (3)
run, and
.B JENT_ERR_SELFTEST
is returned. A permanent failure during the startup of a replacement ends the
recovery at once rather than moving on to the next OSR. If an error is
returned by this function, the Jitter RNG is not safe to be used on the
current system.
.LP
Otherwise the function
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
has the same error codes as
.BR jent_read_entropy ().
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR jent_read_entropy ()
and
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
return the number of bytes generated,
.IR len ,
on success and a negative error code otherwise.
.SH ERRORS
.BR jent_read_entropy ()
and
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
return the number of bytes generated on success or one of the following
negative codes. The health test codes are returned in FIPS or NTG.1 mode only,
except
.B JENT_ERR_RCT_PERMANENT
for a stopped noise source.
Of the intermittent health test codes,
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
returns one only where the platform could not provide a replacement collector,
as described above; the collector is then left as it was and can be used
again.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_EINVAL " (\-1)"
No entropy collector, or no data buffer for a non-zero length.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_RCT " (\-2)"
The SP800-90B repetition count test failed.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_APT " (\-3)"
The SP800-90B adaptive proportion test failed.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_NOTIME " (\-4)"
The internal timer cannot be initialized.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_LAG " (\-5)"
The lag predictor test failed.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_RCT_PERMANENT " (\-6)"
The repetition count test failed permanently.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_APT_PERMANENT " (\-7)"
The adaptive proportion test failed permanently.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_LAG_PERMANENT " (\-8)"
The lag predictor test failed permanently.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_RCT_MEM " (\-9)"
The repetition count test with memory failed.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_RCT_MEM_PERMANENT " (\-10)"
The repetition count test with memory failed permanently.
.TP
.BR JENT_ERR_SELFTEST " (\-11)"
A
.BR jent_selftest (3)
run bound to this instance, or the self test of the conditioning or of the
GCD analysis during a recovery of
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe (),
failed; the failure is permanent, and
.BR jent_status (3)
reports
.I selftestFailed
as
.IR true .
.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
See
.B THREAD SAFETY
in
.BR jitterentropy (3)
for the details.
.ad l
.TS
allbox;
lbx lb
lx l.
Interface	Thread safety
T{
\%\fBjent_read_entropy\fP(), \%\fBjent_read_entropy_safe\fP()
T}	MT-Safe race:entropy_collector
.TE
.ad
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3),
.BR jent_entropy_init (3),
.BR jent_status (3),
.BR jitterentropy (3)
